  "pairing": "fraunces-nunito-sans",
  "typeCharacter": "Fraunces at its heaviest, soft-shouldered weight reads like risen dough and wood-fire warmth. It is set very large in sentence case with tight leading, never italic. Nunito Sans carries running text, menu descriptions and hours at a calm regular weight, with semibold for menu item names.",
  "composition": "Hero, full height on the #181C14 ground. Columns 1–7 hold the h1 in heavy Fraunces at about 7vw in #EDEFE6 across three lines, the lead in Nunito Sans #A9B09A spanning 5 columns, and one rectangular button in #E0632A with dark text and a barely rounded 4px radius. Columns 8–12 are a full-height #C8461E field bled to the top and right edges, and the painted olive branch sits inside it. A thin 1px #3A4330 rule closes the hero. Next comes a ribbon band in #8FA35A carrying four short phrases in dark Fraunces, separated by small olive-leaf ornaments. Menu section on #181C14: the h2 sits in columns 1–4 with its short lead below. Columns 6–12 hold a two-column menu list of the six offerings, each name in semibold #EDEFE6 over a hairline #3A4330 rule; Pica Oljka gets its description line in #A9B09A and a small olive-green leaf mark beside it. Story section is a full-width #C8461E band. Its h2 '48 ur' is display Fraunces at about 12vw in #F1EFE6, spanning columns 1–8. The story text sits in columns 9–12, and a small ink drawing of stacked split firewood sits beneath it. Call section on #23291D surface: the h2 and short text sit in columns 1–5, with the phone as a huge Fraunces numeral in #E0632A below them. Columns 7–12 hold opening hours as a week strip of seven cells, then the address beside a simple schematic line map in #8FA35A showing the street and the marina edge. A small note in #A9B09A states that the restaurant is being renovated. A slim footer on #181C14 closes the page, with the name in Fraunces at left and the address at right.",
  "imagery": "No photographs at all. There are two painted pieces, each on its own plain ground with no text, people or buildings. The first, in the hero, is a single long olive branch with slender leaves and a few dark olives. It is painted in pale sage #DDE3C8 and olive #8FA35A gouache on a flat #C8461E ground, angled diagonally down the ember field. The second, in the story band, is a small loose ink drawing of three stacked split firewood logs in #F1EFE6 line on the flat #C8461E ground. Small olive-leaf ornaments in the ribbon are a simple line drawing.",
  "signature": "The hero's ember-red field bleeding off the right edge like the heat of the open oven, with a pale olive branch painted across it.",
  "copy": {
    "headline": "Pice iz krušne peči na drva, dve minuti od marine",
    "lead": "Testo zori 48 ur, nato pico spečemo na drva. Sedite pri nas v Izoli ali pico odnesite s seboj. Pripravimo tudi testenine z morskimi sadeži, rižote in domač tiramisu."
  },
  "imagePrompt": "One flat full-page screenshot of a desktop restaurant homepage, 1536×1024 px, no browser window, no device frame, no perspective, no photographs anywhere. Page ground is a deep olive-black #181C14. Typography: headings in Fraunces at a heavy, soft, doughy weight in sentence case, never italic; body text in Nunito Sans regular. HERO, filling the first screen on a 12-column grid: the left seven columns carry a huge three-line Fraunces headline in #EDEFE6, a short lead paragraph in #A9B09A below it, then a single rectangular button in ember orange #E0632A with dark #181C14 text and a 4px corner radius. The right five columns are a solid ember-red #C8461E panel bleeding to the top and right page edges. Across it lies a painted gouache olive branch, long and diagonal, with slender pale sage #DDE3C8 and olive #8FA35A leaves and a few dark olives, on the flat red ground. The branch carries no text and has a clear margin around it. A thin #3A4330 rule sits under the hero. BELOW: a narrow full-width ribbon band in olive green #8FA35A with four short phrases in dark Fraunces, separated by tiny line-drawn olive leaves. MENU section on #181C14: the heading and a short lead sit at left in columns 1–4. At right, columns 6–12 hold a two-column menu list of six items, with names in semibold #EDEFE6 and hairline #3A4330 rules between them; one item has a muted #A9B09A description and a tiny olive leaf mark. STORY section is a full-width ember-red #C8461E band, with an enormous Fraunces display heading in #F1EFE6 spanning two thirds of the width. At right sits a short paragraph in #F1EFE6 and, beneath it, a small loose ink line drawing of three stacked split firewood logs in #F1EFE6 on the flat red. CALL section on dark surface #232A1D: the heading and short text sit at left, with a very large Fraunces phone numeral in #E0632A below. At right is a week strip of seven hour cells with thin #3A4330 borders, then the address next to a simple schematic line map in #8FA35A showing a street and the sea edge of a marina, followed by a small muted note. A slim footer on #181C14 closes the page. The style is flat colour with no gradients, no shadows, no pill buttons, no icons, no people, and no left–right symmetry or centring."
}

